The GRUB boot menu theme in usr/share/grub/themes/amethystora follows the
gfxmenu theme layout of grub2-themes by Vince Liuice, licensed under the GNU
General Public License, version 3:

  - grub2-themes  https://github.com/vinceliuice/grub2-themes

Its artwork is Amethystora's own, generated by branding/generate.mjs; no files
from that project are included.

The icon theme in usr/share/icons/candy-icons is candy-icons by Eliver Lara,
licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3:

  - candy-icons  https://github.com/EliverLara/candy-icons

It is installed from upstream by build_files/base/10-icons.sh, which changes the
theme's inheritance, drops the symbolic names outside places/ and adds aliases
for the applications this image ships; the licence ships with it in
usr/share/licenses/candy-icons.

The Amethystora Manual in usr/share/amethystora/manual adapts parts of the
Bluefin documentation, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; the
pages are rewritten for Amethystora:

  - bluefin-docs  https://github.com/ublue-os/bluefin-docs

The manual's window is an Electron app. Electron and marked, which renders the
pages, are installed from their upstream releases by
build_files/base/13-manual.sh, each licensed under the MIT License. Their
licences, and those of the Chromium components Electron includes, ship in
usr/share/licenses/amethystora-manual.

  - Electron  https://github.com/electron/electron
  - marked    https://github.com/markedjs/marked

